  "worked_solution": "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x+164 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+16x & =-164\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x & =-164 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 8x+{8}^{2}-{8}^{2} & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2}-64 & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2} & =-100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8,\\,q=-100,$ and $p+q=-92.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+8)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-100} \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm 10\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-8+10\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-8-10\\,\\text{i}.$",
